          title: 'String and StringBuilder',
          code: 'public class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        // String — immutable\n        String s = "Hello";\n        String s2 = s.concat(" World"); // creates new String\n        System.out.println(s);   // Hello (original unchanged)\n        System.out.println(s2);  // Hello World\n\n        // StringBuilder — mutable\n        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder("Hello");\n        sb.append(" World");\n        sb.reverse();\n        System.out.println(sb.toString()); // dlroW olleH\n\n        // String methods\n        String data = "  Ahmed  ";\n        System.out.println(data.trim());           // Ahmed\n        System.out.println(data.trim().length());  // 5\n        System.out.println(data.contains("Ahmed")); // true\n        System.out.println("Hello".toUpperCase()); // HELLO\n    }\n}',
          language: 'java',
          output: 'Hello\nHello World\ndlroW olleH\nAhmed\n5\ntrue\nHELLO',
